{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
A fresh Kontrol-ID installation uses safe defaults and remains disabled until
it is enabled at Services > Kontrol-ID. Existing settings are preserved during
upgrades. The package manager installs the matching Kontrol Squid and
E2Guardian packages, including their transitive dependencies.

Kontrol-ID cannot coexist with pfSense-pkg-squid or the legacy
Kontrol-pkg-E2guardian5 GUI package because they own the same configuration
files. Remove the conflicting GUI package before installing Kontrol-ID. Do not
remove a shared squid, e2guardian or library package already required by the
matching Kontrol package.

Transparent mode identifies Windows users by source IP and never challenges an
intercepted browser. Explicit proxy mode supports Kerberos/SPNEGO, optional
NTLM compatibility, and Basic authentication through an existing Kontrol
local or LDAP authentication server. Configure and validate AD membership or
import an AES keytab under Services > Kontrol-ID > Domain and Keytab before
enabling Kerberos or NTLM. Kerberos is recommended. If NTLM is enabled, enforce
NTLMv2 and reject LM/NTLMv1 through Active Directory security policy.

For transparent identity, generate an enrollment token under Status and
Enrollment and provision Windows endpoints before enforcement. Domain join
passwords are sent only to kinit over a pipe and are never stored in config.xml.

Runtime databases in /var/db/kontrol-identity and protected domain state in
/var/db/kontrol-id-domain are intentionally preserved when the package is
removed. Winbind is stopped and Squid/E2Guardian integration blocks are removed
by the package deinstall hook.
EOM
}
